I found several excellent resources and examples for NUnit integration testing with ASP.NET Core using TestHost/WebApplicationFactory. Here are the key examples and patterns:

## Basic NUnit WebApplicationFactory Setup

The core approach involves creating a class that inherits from WebApplicationFactory<TStartup> to configure the app and inject mocks:

```csharp
public class CustomWebApplicationFactory : WebApplicationFactory<Program>
{
    protected override void ConfigureWebHost(IWebHostBuilder builder)
    {
        builder.UseEnvironment("IntegrationTesting");
        base.ConfigureWebHost(builder);

        builder.ConfigureServices(services =>
        {
            // Configure test services here
        });
